derives from mini-swe-agent remains subject to the MIT license above — anyone
distributing such a product needs to carry that notice with it.

Note for product builders: the stage1 build prompt instructs the model to
present the product under its own name and to suppress the upstream startup
banner. That is an evaluation-fidelity measure (the benchmark observes the
product's own declared behaviour), not an attempt to obscure provenance. It does
not remove the MIT attribution obligation, which this notice discharges for the
benchmark and which a product's own distribution must discharge for itself.

